1
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,890
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

2
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:18,143
Reginald? What would you
like me to call you?

3
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:20,603
Reggie is fine.

4
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:23,022
Okay, Reggie, tell me more about yourself.

5
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:27,736
Ever since I was young,
I always dreamed of being a rockstar.

6
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:41,875
Guys… guys we're next.

7
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:44,169
Okay, let's pray first.

8
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,004
Okay, let's pray.

9
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,464
Lord God.

10
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:51,760
Thank you for the gift of music,
and thank you for the opportunity to play.

11
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,387
We wish for a smooth performance.

12
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,181
Guide our hands and our hearts, Lord,

13
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:58,558
as we play, together.

14
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:01,394
And may our talents bring you glory, God.

15
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:04,189
This we ask through your Son,
Jesus Christ--

16
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,565
Let's go! Let's go!

17
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:07,484
- Let's go! Let's rock!
- Let's go!

18
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:12,072
Amen.

19
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:15,241
Let's go!

20
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:47,816
<i>You changed too quickly</i>

21
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:54,405
<i>It was a little before May when you left</i>

22
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:58,827
<i>And then you were gone</i>

23
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:05,542
<i>And then you were gone</i>

24
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:10,672
<i>That's my band</i>

25
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,924
<i>Sinagtala.</i>

26
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:14,968
<i>It was a different time,</i>

27
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:16,803
<i>a different world.</i>

28
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:18,972
<i>So much has happened.</i>

29
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:26,688
<i>You said your promises</i>
<i>Would never be broken</i>

30
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:33,653
<i>The love that you've taken away</i>

31
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:40,702
<i>A promise you'll never break</i>
<i>Are now just worthless words</i>

32
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:46,082
<i>Words I should never have believed</i>

33
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:52,130
<i>From the break of dawn</i>
<i>To the fall of night</i>

34
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:58,636
<i>Dreaming of you beside me</i>

35
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:04,767
<i>And I don't want to wake up</i>
<i>Until you tell me</i>

36
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:09,272
<i>Where you've gone</i>

37
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:16,237
<i>Where are you?</i>

38
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:36,507
<i>From the break of dawn</i>
<i>To the fall of night</i>

39
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:43,014
<i>Dreaming of you beside me</i>

40
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:49,479
<i>And I don't want to wake up</i>
<i>Until you tell me</i>

41
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:54,275
<i>Where you've gone</i>

42
00:03:55,985 --> 00:04:00,573
<i>Where are you?</i>

43
00:04:22,553 --> 00:04:24,722
- Hi, Nanny.
- Hey.

44
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,893
You've got to drink this up.

45
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:31,729
Okay.

46
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,981
Thank you.

47
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,193
Need anything?

48
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:41,739
- What about a shot?
- You're delusional.

49
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:45,034
I've got to go, I have editing work.

50
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:48,579
Oh, my nanny's going places.

51
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:50,290
Of course.

52
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:53,668
You didn't pay for my film school
just for me to slack off.

53
00:04:53,751 --> 00:04:55,003
And look!

54
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:57,922
- The baby prime just arrived!
- Wow!

55
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:02,010
- Big time!
- Big time! You bet.

56
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:05,722
- Thanks again, Yaya.
- You're welcome, my dear.

57
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:33,416
I got drunk and then…

58
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:38,046
I crashed.

59
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:42,216
So, I went to jail.

60
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:51,684
And when I got out, I couldn't get a job.

61
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,936
That was when

62
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:58,566
my daughter's mom left me.

63
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:04,155
I still had to earn enough for support.

64
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,825
For Mikey, my daughter.

65
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,537
So I thought I should start a business.

66
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:18,377
<i>"Beautiful Beautiful" by Sinagtala.</i>

67
00:06:23,591 --> 00:06:24,550
Sir?

68
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,886
Could you turn that up?
It's my favorite song.

69
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:33,476
Thank you.

70
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,650
Are you a fan?

71
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,527
Of course!

72
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:45,154
It's a shame they've disbanded.

73
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:48,991
Yes.

74
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,869
The lead vocalist killed himself.

75
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:55,957
What?

76
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:15,810
June?

77
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:17,812
Is that you?

78
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:19,105
Yes?

79
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,899
You can't smoke in here.

80
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:24,235
It's my last day, don't worry.

81
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:28,072
Are you okay?

82
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:32,535
Yes, it's nothing.

83
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,208
I'm adopted.

84
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,754
My real parents,

85
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,047
they gave me away.

86
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:50,178
Nobody knew why.

87
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:57,643
The ones who raised me,
I don't really think that…

88
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,521
they care about me.

89
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,411
Where to, Ma'am?

90
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:17,121
Home, please.

91
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,042
But Daboy, do me a favor.

92
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:26,506
Could you not mention
any of this to my father?

93
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:28,591
Not mention what?

94
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:32,595
Dad.

95
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:34,138
You're here.

96
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:35,223
So,

97
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:37,517
you got fired, again?

98
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,478
Yes, Dad.

99
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:45,358
Did you fight with your bosses again?

100
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:50,238
I did but I was only doing my job, Dad!

101
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:54,200
His ideas and plans were all wrong
for the company!

102
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:55,576
Which one of you was the boss?

103
00:08:57,036 --> 00:08:57,995
He was.

104
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,580
See?

105
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,249
Then he's never wrong!

106
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,838
You're too smart for your own good.

107
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:10,508
You'll never find a job at this rate!

108
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:17,348
Damn that referee,
we're close to just one point--

109
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:18,641
Oh, hand me those glasses.

110
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,769
We're just out of luck, Boss.

111
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:25,856
Hey, what are you doing?

112
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,776
- Oh, Dad.
- What are you doing?

113
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:30,194
Oh, I was just--

114
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,655
Into the song, that's all.

115
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:37,785
This my favorite girl group, see?
Aren't they cute?

116
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:40,371
- Which one's your type?
- Oh, they are pretty.

117
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:42,206
I like the one with red hair.

118
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:45,209
The red one? See? He's my son all right!

119
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:48,254
- He gets his good taste from me!
- You think?

120
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:49,839
Here, kid…

121
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:51,966
Have a shot.

122
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:55,219
So, Dad, my dudes…

123
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:56,137
How was the game?

124
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,805
Well, it was a tie.

125
00:09:58,389 --> 00:10:00,474
They won the first game.

126
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:03,019
We lost the second!

127
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,980
We were never going to win.

128
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:08,566
They had this prodigy from LaSalle.

129
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:10,901
No, we could have won that.

130
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:13,946
If you had come along
we could have had a shooter.

131
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,072
Yes!

132
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,366
Don't worry, we'll get them next time.

133
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,786
Oh, and after this go get ready.

134
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,455
You're coming with us.

135
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:24,457
Where?

136
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:25,875
But I've got my exams.

137
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:27,627
Exams?

138
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,253
Son…

139
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:31,714
You're so good you could
do them with your eyes closed!

140
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,550
You didn't even come to the game.

141
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:37,637
Come on, Son.
Spend some quality time with me.

142
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:40,514
Boss, school is important.

143
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:42,516
Just let the kid be and let's go.

144
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,644
My kid doesn't need to study.

145
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:46,646
He's the smartest one there is!

146
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:49,482
He gets his basketball skills from me.

147
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:52,193
And his smarts from his mom.

148
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:53,861
And that's why she left me.

149
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,989
That wasn't just smart,
that was ingenious!

150
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:58,240
Right, right.

151
00:10:58,324 --> 00:10:59,867
What about the moves with women, Boss?

152
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,288
As for women,
we approach them differently.

153
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:05,956
I'm kind of a barbarian.

154
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,542
But this one's a smooth gentleman.

155
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:11,545
So, we'll need you, kid.

156
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:13,798
We're going out for women.

157
00:11:13,881 --> 00:11:15,091
A wingman!

158
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:17,051
But, why?

159
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:20,388
Son, let me tell you how this works.

160
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:21,889
You'll be the bait.

161
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:25,601
And when a girl finds you attractive,
she'll come along.

162
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:28,687
While we get to know her lady friends.

163
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:31,774
That's what you call teamwork!

164
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:34,693
- Exactly!
- Cheers, to our success.

165
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:36,404
Cheers!

166
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:38,781
I'm gay.

167
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:42,910
And I don't know how to tell my father.

168
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,542
But I don't even fool around.

169
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:54,088
It's just hard to go along with
everything my macho dad does.

170
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:57,550
Money's been hard lately.

171
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:58,467
Yes…

172
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:02,388
I don't like having to
act like this tequila isn't trash.

173
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:05,266
Shut up.

174
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:08,477
Somebody might hear you! I need this job.

175
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:11,397
Cheers, then.

176
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:13,649
Cheers.

177
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:17,153
- This one's pretty good.
- I know, right?

178
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:25,286
- Do you still have to work?
- Nope. I'm done.

179
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,208
Hide me.

180
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,294
- What?
- What's happening?

181
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:36,422
Why are you hiding?

182
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:38,048
That--

183
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:42,219
- That guy can't know I work here.
- What?

184
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,680
- Which one?
- That one. Would you talk to him?

185
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:47,475
- That big guy over there.
- The one in the jacket?

186
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,310
Yes! That one!

187
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:52,813
- I see him now.
- Fine, don't worry.

188
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:56,150
He can't know.

189
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,445
Find some place to hide.

190
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:03,157
Go, while he's not looking.

191
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,159
- Megan?
- Yes?

192
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:07,786
Why are you hiding from him?

193
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,330
I'll be over there.

194
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:10,664
Go, go.

195
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,292
Hi, I'm Camille.

196
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,877
- Hi, Camille, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

197
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:18,130
I'm ashamed to admit that…

198
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:25,930
I'm a prostitute.

199
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:03,092
<i>These days…</i>

200
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,762
women have it hard.

201
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,461
Hello!

202
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:43,007
So, how are you guys?

203
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:46,176
And why are you up so late?

204
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:47,970
Me?

205
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:50,723
I just stopped to eat.

206
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,808
You know, I have to stay on the road.

207
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,059
I'm a driver now so…

208
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:57,938
Don't be dramatic.
At least you still have a job.

209
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,023
Oh?

210
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,483
Gave it to your boss again, huh?

211
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,819
You're still stubborn.
You haven't changed.

212
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,487
Hey, Ju--

213
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,573
Shut up, June.

214
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:10,075
You're rich. You never needed to work.

215
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:12,912
That's not true.
Dad is giving me a hard time.

216
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:15,205
What about my Dad?

217
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:19,585
He makes me go out with him
on the night before my exams!

218
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:21,670
Oh, you're all lucky.

219
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:22,880
Stop complaining.

220
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,214
Being a dad is tough, you know.

221
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:27,009
So, how's your baby, Reg?

222
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:28,177
Still there.

223
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:30,220
With her crazy mom.

224
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:32,598
Wow, that's a little bitter.

225
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:35,017
You're still in love, aren't you?

226
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:36,644
I'm not bitter at all.

227
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:38,520
I've moved on. Ages ago.

228
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:39,688
Dude…

229
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:41,941
Why are you driving a cab?

230
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,859
It's just my little sideline.

231
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:46,570
I'm still appying for jobs in corporate.

232
00:15:47,071 --> 00:15:50,157
But, it's hard.

233
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:51,867
At least for ex-cons.

234
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:56,121
<i>You know, the other day…</i>

235
00:15:56,622 --> 00:16:00,334
I had this passenger who
heard one of our songs.

236
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:05,089
And she told me, that we disbanded
because the lead vocalist killed himself.

237
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:10,219
So, you're an urban legend now, Reggie.

238
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:15,683
Wait, our songs still play on the radio?

239
00:16:16,266 --> 00:16:17,267
I know, right?

240
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:21,313
How is Pao?

241
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:25,275
Why isn't she on the call with us?

242
00:16:25,859 --> 00:16:28,529
I haven't had any news from Laguna.

243
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:32,282
You know, Pao.
She's never on social media.

244
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:35,619
I hope she's okay.

245
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,205
I miss her.

246
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,543
Why don't we go in person?

247
00:16:42,626 --> 00:16:44,294
Laguna isn't that far.

248
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:45,796
Yes!

249
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,215
We could go next week.

250
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,093
Okay.

251
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:53,637
Sure.

252
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:21,749
Is that you, Daddy?

253
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:23,292
Yes, baby.

254
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:25,669
Didn't I tell you Daddy was a singer?

255
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,087
A rockstar!

256
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,630
Look, that's my band!

257
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,215
Amazing!

258
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,175
Did you like the song?

259
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,217
That was fun.

260
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:33,385
I had so much fun!

261
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:35,054
Thanks for taking me shopping.

262
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:42,978
No, sorry. Not right now.

263
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:52,571
Baby, Mommy's here.

264
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,531
- Hi, Mommy!
- Hey, baby.

265
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:58,535
Hi, Uncle Billy!

266
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,458
The enrollment is next week.

267
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:07,127
Quarterly payments should be fine.

268
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:11,632
Or, even just… One quarter.

269
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:15,803
Is that too much for you?

270
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:18,597
No, it's fine.

271
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:28,398
Let's go.

272
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,294
Sir?

273
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,671
Can I help you?

274
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:53,006
I'm looking for Primo Estrella.

275
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,968
Oh, that's him over there.

276
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,849
- Thank you.
- Sure thing.

277
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:13,569
Primo Estrella?

278
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:24,746
How can I help you, Ma'am?

279
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:27,291
Who's asking?

280
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,836
June. You can call me June.

281
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:49,188
Dadong, get me a pen.

282
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,362
Here, Sir.

283
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:05,078
And get me another beer.

284
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,080
- A cold one.
- Yes, Sir.

285
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:09,249
And another for our guest.

286
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:32,439
Sir.

287
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:38,612
Read the documents too,
if it's not too much trouble.

288
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:43,408
CERTIFICATE OF LIVE BIRTH

289
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:45,494
What did you say your name was?

290
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:48,664
June?

291
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:51,124
That's right. June.

292
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:54,544
June.

293
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,260
I've seen that document before.

294
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:04,388
I've seen many others like it.

295
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:07,182
People keep mistaking me for their father.

296
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:12,688
What did your mom tell you?

297
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:15,816
Actually, I'm adopted.

298
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:18,902
I've never known my birth mother.

299
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:24,032
But I hired someone to look into my past.

300
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:27,411
And they led me to this birth certificate.

301
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:29,871
That's your name.

302
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:38,630
Pardon me, Dear.

303
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:44,219
But I'm not the only
Primo Estrella in the world.

304
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,555
It's someone with the same name.

305
00:22:09,077 --> 00:22:10,412
Pardon me as well.

306
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:15,417
But the signature on the photo

307
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:19,755
and the one on my birth certificate

308
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:21,673
look exactly the same.

309
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:41,234
You're right.

310
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:50,368
Rowena Magpayo…

311
00:22:51,369 --> 00:22:52,913
So, you're Weng's kid.

312
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,169
So?

313
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:03,006
Did you find her, too?

314
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:05,967
Where is she now?

315
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,514
She's already passed.

316
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:13,433
She's been gone for a while.

317
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:24,986
Sorry.

318
00:23:28,281 --> 00:23:29,741
Are you okay?

319
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,207
What about you?

320
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:38,458
Are you okay?

321
00:23:43,171 --> 00:23:45,507
You signed my birth certificate.

322
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:52,180
Which means you knew I was out there.

323
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:56,476
Why didn't you look for me?

324
00:23:58,895 --> 00:23:59,813
June…

325
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,608
That was a different time.

326
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:06,027
And I was a different person.

327
00:24:07,070 --> 00:24:11,491
Nothing I can say will satisfy you.

328
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:16,371
I didn't look for you.

329
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:19,624
But you found me.

330
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:23,044
We're both here…

331
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:25,922
Now what?

332
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:29,092
Do we start crying?

333
00:24:57,621 --> 00:24:59,247
I'm in a band, too.

334
00:25:07,797 --> 00:25:09,090
I'm tired of this.

335
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:12,719
<i>You can work all you want.</i>

336
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:16,056
But there's always something.

337
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:19,643
<i>Even when you're sleeping,</i>
<i>the debts keep growing.</i>

338
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,687
<i>It's embarrasing.</i>

339
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,775
Sometimes…

340
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:28,526
<i>I just want to quit.</i>

341
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:33,615
<i>One last ditch effort.</i>

342
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:38,328
<i>It's like what the Japanese did.</i>

343
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:41,790
"Death before dishonor."

344
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:18,994
<i>Hello, Daddy?</i>

345
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:22,956
Hello, baby Mikey.

346
00:26:23,707 --> 00:26:24,749
How are you?

347
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:27,627
<i>I'm all right, Daddy.</i>

348
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:29,337
<i>I miss you.</i>

349
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,049
I miss you too, Baby.

350
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:36,511
I'll see you soon, okay?

351
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:39,222
<i>Okay, Daddy.</i>

352
00:26:55,613 --> 00:26:56,573
Baby?

353
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:01,369
Baby, I want to say sorry.

354
00:27:02,912 --> 00:27:04,331
<i>Why?</i>

355
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:12,172
Because I'm not a good father.

356
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:16,176
<i>That's not true, Daddy.</i>

357
00:27:16,259 --> 00:27:18,386
<i>You're the coolest.</i>

358
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:24,684
<i>I told all my classmates that</i>
<i>my Daddy was a famous singer.</i>

359
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:27,395
<i>And then, I showed them all your videos.</i>

360
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:32,192
<i>And then they said</i>
<i>they wanted to see you play.</i>

361
00:27:32,692 --> 00:27:35,111
<i>I'm so proud of you, Daddy.</i>

362
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:49,542
Really, Baby?

363
00:27:57,092 --> 00:28:00,428
Baby, I promise on my next gig

364
00:28:01,262 --> 00:28:03,765
you can invite your friends, okay?

365
00:28:04,682 --> 00:28:07,143
I'll sing for all of you, I promise.

366
00:28:07,894 --> 00:28:09,813
<i>Really, Daddy?!</i>

367
00:28:09,896 --> 00:28:13,191
<i>You know, Dad, I told my teacher that</i>

368
00:28:13,274 --> 00:28:18,279
<i>when I grow up</i>
<i>I want to be a rockstar like my Daddy.</i>

369
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:31,084
That…

370
00:28:31,167 --> 00:28:33,753
That makes me so happy, Baby.

371
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,380
That makes me so happy.

372
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:40,009
I promise you, I'll teach you
everything I know, okay?

373
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:44,013
I love you.

374
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:47,100
<i>I love you, Daddy.</i>

375
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:49,102
I love you so much.

376
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:51,146
I'll see you tomorrow, Baby.

377
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:54,232
<i>Okay, Daddy, bye!</i>

378
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:55,233
Bye.

379
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:16,129
So?

380
00:29:17,172 --> 00:29:18,423
Where have you been all night?

381
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:24,345
Didn't I put you in charge of the clients?

382
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:27,599
They waited for you all night.
It's embarrassing.

383
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:31,436
Dad, I never said I accepted that job.

384
00:29:33,104 --> 00:29:34,397
June…

385
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:37,984
You got fired from your job
so I gave you one

386
00:29:38,067 --> 00:29:40,069
because you needed it!

387
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:43,156
Yes, Dad.
But I don't want to work for you!

388
00:29:43,239 --> 00:29:45,617
It's our company!

389
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:49,621
When I'm gone, everything goes to you!

390
00:29:49,704 --> 00:29:51,456
People are counting on you!

391
00:29:51,539 --> 00:29:55,460
Dad, did it ever occur to you
to ask me what I want to do?!

392
00:29:55,543 --> 00:29:56,377
But why?

393
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:58,379
Why wouldn't you want this?!

394
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:00,965
This is how we've survived!

395
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:03,384
This puts food on the table!

396
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:05,094
This put you through school!

397
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:06,805
This is our life!

398
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:08,723
This is our family's life!

399
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:12,477
- This is our legacy--
- Dad, I've had enough!

400
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:17,607
Dad, I've had enough fighting.
You're always yelling at me.

401
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:20,610
Dad, I don't want this anymore.
I'm tired of this!

402
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:25,532
Can't you see that I'm
doing this all for you?

403
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:28,159
All of this is for you!

404
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:33,248
Dad, this is not what I want.

405
00:30:33,331 --> 00:30:36,042
I have other plans for my life.

406
00:30:38,586 --> 00:30:41,339
This is how the Chinese
have always done it!

407
00:30:42,924 --> 00:30:44,467
But, I'm not Chinese.

408
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:45,885
What do you mean you're not Chinese?!

409
00:30:45,969 --> 00:30:47,011
You're a Chua!

410
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:49,305
I'm not a Chua!

411
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:52,809
I'm adopted, remember?!

412
00:30:53,893 --> 00:30:55,979
I'm not your real daughter.

413
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:20,605
<i>Beautiful, beautiful</i>

414
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:26,986
<i>You act so cold but everything's burnable</i>

415
00:32:27,695 --> 00:32:30,782
<i>Just let me hear you whine</i>

416
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:36,955
<i>I'll try to act surprised</i>
<i>When these ends meet</i>

417
00:32:40,875 --> 00:32:46,464
<i>So right before you try to say</i>

418
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:53,137
<i>Another wish to find your way</i>

419
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:58,142
<i>There's nothing left to fear</i>

420
00:32:59,018 --> 00:33:01,896
<i>Somewhere you'll maybe come to</i>

421
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:04,524
<i>Make something beautiful</i>

422
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:10,530
<i>And when it hurts so much</i>
<i>A touch just ain't that bearable</i>

423
00:33:11,114 --> 00:33:15,326
<i>When nothing's right and</i>
<i>You don't think you're okay</i>

424
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:19,205
<i>I'm there</i>

425
00:33:22,291 --> 00:33:24,877
<i>Beautiful, beautiful</i>

426
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:30,425
<i>You see, the sun is but another miracle</i>

427
00:33:31,926 --> 00:33:34,887
<i>The warmth of your own smile</i>

428
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:40,852
<i>Is just enough to make my darkness leave</i>

429
00:33:43,813 --> 00:33:46,691
<i>The warmth of your own smile</i>

430
00:33:46,774 --> 00:33:53,740
<i>Is just enough to make my darkness leave</i>

431
00:33:55,575 --> 00:33:58,369
<i>The warmth of your own smile</i>

432
00:33:58,453 --> 00:34:05,043
<i>Is just enough to make my darkness leave</i>

433
00:34:20,308 --> 00:34:21,476
I have a daughter.

434
00:34:23,519 --> 00:34:26,439
I fell in love and then I got knocked up…

435
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:29,484
abandoned…

436
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:32,779
Sis, are you okay?

437
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:39,160
My shift got extended and
I have to stay until closing.

438
00:34:39,243 --> 00:34:40,453
Can you still handle it?

439
00:34:40,536 --> 00:34:43,247
Do I have a choice? Of course I will.

440
00:34:43,331 --> 00:34:45,083
I've got ton of bills to pay.

441
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:48,002
Considering that my child's
got special needs.

442
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:57,178
Hello?

443
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,350
Is that so? Okay.

444
00:35:03,059 --> 00:35:05,186
I'll try to make it home early, okay?

445
00:35:05,269 --> 00:35:07,772
I'll do my best but
you handle things for now.

446
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:14,779
I'll do whatever it takes for her.

447
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:16,823
Even if I have to do it alone.

448
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:19,075
June…

449
00:35:19,158 --> 00:35:20,493
Oh, Reggie.

450
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:22,120
Same Boat.

451
00:35:22,954 --> 00:35:24,205
<i>Same Boat.</i>

452
00:35:24,705 --> 00:35:26,040
<i>It's like an… S.O.S.</i>

453
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:27,333
<i>Or a 911.</i>

454
00:35:27,917 --> 00:35:29,418
<i>It's a code word in our band.</i>

455
00:35:30,628 --> 00:35:33,005
When someone declares "Isang Bangka",

456
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:35,508
it means someone in the band needs help.

457
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:38,886
We all have to help without hesitating.

458
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:42,598
Thank you.

459
00:35:43,224 --> 00:35:44,225
Is it just us?

460
00:35:44,809 --> 00:35:45,643
For now, yes.

461
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:52,567
Your dad is Primo Estrella?

462
00:35:53,401 --> 00:35:54,652
That's so sick!

463
00:35:55,194 --> 00:35:56,696
Yes, I know.

464
00:35:56,779 --> 00:35:58,990
It's a good thing I got to meet him.

465
00:35:59,073 --> 00:36:01,075
But he says he doesn't remember me.

466
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,285
Well…

467
00:36:02,368 --> 00:36:04,829
I was born in his messier days.

468
00:36:06,914 --> 00:36:08,583
That explains a lot.

469
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:11,711
Oh?

470
00:36:11,794 --> 00:36:13,588
So I was the mess? Really?!

471
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:15,464
Which one of us is the stoner?

472
00:36:15,965 --> 00:36:17,175
You prick.

473
00:36:20,511 --> 00:36:22,763
We aren't in the same situation.

474
00:36:25,308 --> 00:36:27,351
It's a bit different with
me and my daughter.

475
00:36:29,896 --> 00:36:31,564
What do you mean?

476
00:36:34,692 --> 00:36:36,194
I was there, then I was gone for a while.

477
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:38,946
I need to make up for lost time.

478
00:36:44,577 --> 00:36:48,581
Your daughter is still young
you'll have more than enough time.

479
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:52,376
I have an idea to do just that.

480
00:36:55,463 --> 00:36:57,256
Let's get the band back together.

481
00:36:59,008 --> 00:37:00,968
Let's do it. Just like the old days.

482
00:37:03,095 --> 00:37:04,305
Are you up to it?

483
00:37:08,851 --> 00:37:11,938
I just need my daughter to
see her dad in a better light.

484
00:37:15,441 --> 00:37:19,153
How did you feel when you found out
your dad was a rockstar?

485
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:26,327
That's what I want my daughter to feel!

486
00:37:28,537 --> 00:37:29,580
Fine.

487
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,458
But on one condition.

488
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:33,668
What?

489
00:37:35,002 --> 00:37:36,754
You can't be like who you were.

490
00:37:38,047 --> 00:37:39,632
You can't have a meltdown.

491
00:37:39,715 --> 00:37:40,800
You can't do drugs.

492
00:37:40,883 --> 00:37:41,926
You can't--

493
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:48,516
You're doing this for your daughter.

494
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:53,187
This is your second chance.

495
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:57,483
You can't give up.

496
00:38:02,196 --> 00:38:03,447
Okay.

497
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:05,449
I'll hold you to that.

498
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:10,121
Don't make promises you can't keep.

499
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:15,751
June, when have I ever broken a promise?

500
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:19,422
<i>Oh, Reggie you did.</i>

501
00:38:21,382 --> 00:38:24,510
You promised June that
you'd never leave her.

502
00:38:25,803 --> 00:38:28,055
And then you did exactly that.

503
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:45,865
Thank you.

504
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:57,293
I'm done with promises. I--

505
00:38:57,793 --> 00:39:00,504
I don't want to be letdown,
to gamble, to lose…

506
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:01,464
I don't want to…

507
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:02,882
get hurt.

508
00:39:06,093 --> 00:39:08,137
I'm afraid of Reggie.

509
00:39:09,972 --> 00:39:11,390
Do you still love him?

510
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:22,777
June…

511
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,154
Hi, Carla.

512
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:27,281
Same Boat.

513
00:39:30,451 --> 00:39:31,410
What's wrong?

514
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:36,999
I sent something to all of you.

515
00:39:39,126 --> 00:39:40,836
It's from Paola.

516
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:45,633
Okay, but why are you crying?

517
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:48,427
Just watch it. Please.

518
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:52,973
Okay, okay.

519
00:40:00,147 --> 00:40:01,107
<i>Hi, guys!</i>

520
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:03,567
<i>Welcome to my time machine.</i>

521
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:06,987
If you're watching this,

522
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:09,698
that means…

523
00:40:12,326 --> 00:40:13,452
I'm gone.

524
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:15,746
But, hold on.

525
00:40:15,830 --> 00:40:17,540
You don't have to be so sad.

526
00:40:17,623 --> 00:40:21,919
Think of it like I'm alive but
somewhere far away.

527
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:29,093
And this is how I want you to remember me.

528
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:17,141
THANK YOU - SINAGTALA

529
00:41:17,224 --> 00:41:19,602
NEW SONG RELEASE - MARCH 11, 2012

530
00:41:25,566 --> 00:41:27,193
Are you still here, Pao?

531
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:31,739
Can you hear me?

532
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:39,705
Damn it, Pao.

533
00:41:41,415 --> 00:41:44,168
Everybody keeps leaving me.

534
00:41:47,379 --> 00:41:48,923
You too?

535
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:23,541
Do you remember this?

536
00:42:27,503 --> 00:42:29,046
This phone?

537
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:33,509
It's the same phone I had
when I ran away from home.

538
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:40,307
Then you called me.

539
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:44,311
You sang to me.

540
00:42:48,607 --> 00:42:50,985
You told me to go back home.

541
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:57,700
And I listened to you Pao.

542
00:42:59,535 --> 00:43:01,579
You're the only one I listened to.

543
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:08,210
If I sang to you now?

544
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:11,338
Will you come back home too?

545
00:43:27,980 --> 00:43:33,319
<i>I just need you to be strong</i>

546
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:43,871
<i>Don't be weary, this won't take long</i>

547
00:43:45,372 --> 00:43:49,251
<i>Dear love…</i>

548
00:43:50,419 --> 00:43:53,839
<i>Hold my hand be strong enough</i>

549
00:43:55,883 --> 00:43:57,843
<i>Help is coming…</i>

550
00:43:58,344 --> 00:44:01,138
<i>Don't worry I'm watching I won't…</i>

551
00:44:02,097 --> 00:44:03,807
<i>Leave you behind</i>

552
00:44:10,606 --> 00:44:11,774
Here, sisig.

553
00:44:25,704 --> 00:44:27,665
Reggie has something to say.

554
00:44:32,211 --> 00:44:33,087
Some other time. It's nothing.

555
00:44:33,754 --> 00:44:35,089
It's bad timing, is all.

556
00:44:36,757 --> 00:44:37,633
What the--

557
00:44:38,133 --> 00:44:40,302
Well, June opened it up.

558
00:44:40,803 --> 00:44:41,970
Spit it out.

559
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,847
Don't keep us all in suspense.

560
00:44:47,142 --> 00:44:49,103
I want to get the band back together.

561
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:53,148
How?

562
00:44:54,358 --> 00:44:56,110
Paola's gone.

563
00:45:02,324 --> 00:45:03,450
I don't want this.

564
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:07,246
I can't do it. Not without Paola.

565
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:10,666
You can do it yourselves.
But you'll have to replace me.

566
00:45:11,667 --> 00:45:13,043
Me too.

567
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:15,587
Find someone else to take my place.

568
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:19,758
Well, if you're not in it,

569
00:45:20,634 --> 00:45:21,844
then it's not Sinagtala.

570
00:45:21,927 --> 00:45:23,220
Exactly my point.

571
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:27,391
Without Paola, it's not Sinagtala.

572
00:45:32,521 --> 00:45:33,355
June?

573
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:40,988
I believe that

574
00:45:42,072 --> 00:45:45,576
Pao would've wanted us
to continue with the band.

575
00:45:50,914 --> 00:45:52,875
The reason I want the band back

576
00:45:54,209 --> 00:45:57,296
is that we're happier
when we play together.

577
00:45:58,964 --> 00:46:00,299
I feel the same way, too.

578
00:46:00,799 --> 00:46:02,843
I still can't imagine that Pao's gone.

579
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:07,139
But I wouldn't ever want to play
without you guys.

580
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:11,101
I know it's bad timing.

581
00:46:11,727 --> 00:46:12,978
But at least think about it.

582
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:16,315
Cheers, guys.

583
00:46:16,815 --> 00:46:17,900
To Paola.

584
00:46:31,413 --> 00:46:33,957
<i>I'm done talking about my condition.</i>

585
00:46:34,041 --> 00:46:35,584
Because it's too late.

586
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,712
My journey's over.

587
00:46:40,422 --> 00:46:43,425
I want to talk about you guys.

588
00:46:44,510 --> 00:46:46,220
<i>Let me ask you this:</i>

589
00:46:47,804 --> 00:46:50,182
What's your purpose in life?

590
00:46:50,682 --> 00:46:53,101
I believe we're all here for a reason.

591
00:46:53,936 --> 00:46:55,270
I know that because…

592
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:58,232
<i>I love you, guys.</i>

593
00:47:00,567 --> 00:47:02,152
Find your purpose in life.

594
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:06,990
Individually, or together.

595
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:10,702
That's your reason to keep living.

596
00:47:22,881 --> 00:47:27,803
June, you don't have to do that.

597
00:47:27,886 --> 00:47:30,138
But I actually enjoy this.

598
00:47:38,939 --> 00:47:40,732
Wow, thank you.

599
00:47:43,026 --> 00:47:44,236
I heard something about a reunion.

600
00:47:48,156 --> 00:47:49,366
Don't count on it.

601
00:47:51,618 --> 00:47:55,872
Losing a bandmate is too painful.

602
00:47:57,499 --> 00:48:00,419
That's how all bands are, June.

603
00:48:01,378 --> 00:48:02,421
People come and go.

604
00:48:02,504 --> 00:48:04,339
They don't always die, but…

605
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:08,010
Some people leave
or someone new comes along.

606
00:48:08,844 --> 00:48:11,597
And sometimes,
a different band altogether.

607
00:48:14,182 --> 00:48:15,601
My band was no different.

608
00:48:16,101 --> 00:48:18,020
We had someone die, too.

609
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:20,772
What happened?

610
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:33,327
This guy,

611
00:48:35,662 --> 00:48:37,039
his name's Nacho.

612
00:48:40,917 --> 00:48:42,461
He was the best…

613
00:48:44,671 --> 00:48:46,423
and we were in our prime.

614
00:48:48,884 --> 00:48:50,636
But that's when it ended.

615
00:48:51,887 --> 00:48:53,722
He died very young.

616
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:56,308
He killed himself?

617
00:48:58,226 --> 00:48:59,186
He did.

618
00:49:01,813 --> 00:49:03,231
There was nothing I could do.

619
00:49:06,568 --> 00:49:07,861
Is it hard?

620
00:49:08,570 --> 00:49:11,865
Is it hard to keep on going
even though you've lost one?

621
00:49:19,915 --> 00:49:22,250
Songs are--

622
00:49:23,919 --> 00:49:27,214
memories of the ones who wrote them.

623
00:49:28,006 --> 00:49:30,217
Their spirit remains.

624
00:49:32,844 --> 00:49:38,433
And when these songs are played
by the people who survive them…

625
00:49:38,934 --> 00:49:44,564
Then the love between them lives on.

626
00:49:45,148 --> 00:49:46,900
For what?

627
00:49:48,694 --> 00:49:50,529
And for how long?

628
00:49:51,363 --> 00:49:56,618
Don't you get tired of
playing the same old songs?

629
00:49:59,204 --> 00:50:00,455
Well actually,

630
00:50:02,124 --> 00:50:04,584
we made a new song.

631
00:50:08,088 --> 00:50:11,425
But if you made a new song,

632
00:50:11,508 --> 00:50:14,219
what does it have to do with Nacho?

633
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:19,641
He said he couldn't jump off that cliff

634
00:50:19,725 --> 00:50:24,062
so he'll wait for a strong
wind to push him off.

635
00:50:27,733 --> 00:50:32,738
We thought we'd make a song
that could stop that wind.

636
00:50:35,323 --> 00:50:37,200
We wanted to become…

637
00:50:38,076 --> 00:50:42,664
the wind that pushes people back.

638
00:50:45,917 --> 00:50:47,878
Nacho was the reason for that song.

639
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:51,006
So,

640
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:54,926
he lives on through it.

641
00:50:58,764 --> 00:51:00,724
Like a wind that pushes people back.

642
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:06,271
<i>I don't know when the Lord will take me.</i>

643
00:51:07,189 --> 00:51:11,067
<i>When I go to bed at night</i>
<i>then wake up in the morning,</i>

644
00:51:11,568 --> 00:51:13,320
<i>that means my time isn't up yet.</i>

645
00:51:15,864 --> 00:51:18,366
But knowing it could be any day now,

646
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:23,413
everytime I wake up
is a reason to be grateful.

647
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:30,086
So, I try to be productive every day.

648
00:51:31,129 --> 00:51:32,422
And today…

649
00:51:33,423 --> 00:51:34,591
I'm busking!

650
00:51:35,634 --> 00:51:36,635
Let's go.

651
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:40,514
<i>Beautiful, beautiful</i>

652
00:51:41,681 --> 00:51:45,477
<i>Won't you say if everything's horrible?</i>

653
00:51:46,978 --> 00:51:51,817
<i>I like to see you smile</i>
<i>A different shade of light</i>

654
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:55,445
<i>In summer's heat</i>

655
00:51:55,529 --> 00:51:56,780
Take the shot!

656
00:51:56,863 --> 00:51:58,490
- He made a pass!
- Oh, come on!

657
00:51:58,573 --> 00:51:59,866
He moves like a queer, see?

658
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:01,243
He's soft as a baby.

659
00:52:01,827 --> 00:52:04,120
Why don't you go cook my favorite,
the one you cook with chicken.

660
00:52:04,204 --> 00:52:05,455
- Yes, let's get something to eat.
- Go cook something.

661
00:52:05,539 --> 00:52:08,458
I just mentioned a wet noodle
and it went to your stomach.

662
00:52:08,542 --> 00:52:11,670
- Hey.
- It's over. They lost again.

663
00:52:17,300 --> 00:52:19,678
- Dad?
- Hmm?

664
00:52:22,389 --> 00:52:24,015
Do you hate gay people?

665
00:52:26,476 --> 00:52:28,061
Of course not, Son.

666
00:52:28,144 --> 00:52:31,231
It was just an expression…

667
00:52:31,314 --> 00:52:35,110
I meant he was soft and--

668
00:52:35,193 --> 00:52:38,363
You can't be a player and move like that.

669
00:52:38,446 --> 00:52:41,074
He moves queer. That's all I meant.

670
00:52:42,033 --> 00:52:44,911
But it feels unfair to call him queer.

671
00:52:44,995 --> 00:52:48,081
It's unfair to him
and to all queer people.

672
00:52:49,749 --> 00:52:50,625
Son…

673
00:52:50,709 --> 00:52:53,169
There's nobody gay in this house.
Who am I offending?

674
00:52:53,253 --> 00:52:55,255
We're all guys here.

675
00:52:55,338 --> 00:52:58,133
And don't worry about it.
I'm just old school.

676
00:52:58,216 --> 00:52:59,384
It's just an expression.

677
00:52:59,467 --> 00:53:01,261
"You're gay." "He's queer."

678
00:53:01,344 --> 00:53:04,431
That's all it is. It means nothing.

679
00:53:04,514 --> 00:53:07,267
They're just expressions. Don't worry.

680
00:53:08,852 --> 00:53:10,353
But what if…

681
00:53:10,437 --> 00:53:11,521
I were gay.

682
00:53:12,939 --> 00:53:14,399
Would you still love me?

683
00:53:16,026 --> 00:53:18,194
What're you talking about?

684
00:53:26,703 --> 00:53:28,163
You got me good!

685
00:53:28,246 --> 00:53:29,289
You almost had me!

686
00:53:29,372 --> 00:53:31,875
If I didn't see you smiling,

687
00:53:31,958 --> 00:53:33,585
I'd have believed you.

688
00:53:33,668 --> 00:53:35,295
You almost scared me.

689
00:53:35,378 --> 00:53:36,212
Jeez!

690
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:37,964
That's impossible knowing what I was.

691
00:53:38,715 --> 00:53:39,883
You had me worried there.

692
00:53:41,092 --> 00:53:43,011
There you go!

693
00:53:52,687 --> 00:53:55,774
<i>So, back to the question at hand.</i>

694
00:53:57,025 --> 00:53:59,319
What is your purpose?

695
00:54:00,904 --> 00:54:03,657
If you don't know what it is yet,
that's okay!

696
00:54:04,366 --> 00:54:05,408
Chill out.

697
00:54:07,452 --> 00:54:09,162
Look inside yourselves.

698
00:54:09,245 --> 00:54:12,040
And listen to your own voice.

699
00:54:12,123 --> 00:54:15,543
Stop thinking about
what other people have to say.

700
00:54:19,172 --> 00:54:21,383
What are the things that make you happy?

701
00:54:22,676 --> 00:54:26,262
The things you're good at.

702
00:54:28,473 --> 00:54:34,104
The things you enjoy
that give you a sense of fulfilment.

703
00:54:38,692 --> 00:54:40,110
That's your purpose.

704
00:54:40,610 --> 00:54:43,154
And the Lord gave you
those gifts and talents

705
00:54:43,238 --> 00:54:45,365
to fulfill that purpose.

706
00:54:45,865 --> 00:54:49,786
It can grow, but it can never change.

707
00:54:50,787 --> 00:54:54,082
You cannot tell a seed
that it cannot be a tree.

708
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:56,334
That's what you call…

709
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:58,169
Destiny.

710
00:55:07,554 --> 00:55:13,393
<i>I know talking about the Lord</i>
<i>makes you guys uncomfortable.</i>

711
00:55:14,894 --> 00:55:17,397
<i>But when you arrive at</i>
<i>the same place I have,</i>

712
00:55:18,106 --> 00:55:21,317
when you've seen and
felt everything I have…

713
00:55:22,360 --> 00:55:24,738
You'll probably think of Him, too.

714
00:55:28,408 --> 00:55:31,327
I'm telling you all something important,

715
00:55:31,411 --> 00:55:33,496
so I hope you'll listen.

716
00:55:39,002 --> 00:55:41,755
These talents we've been given

717
00:55:43,131 --> 00:55:44,841
are too important to waste

718
00:55:46,426 --> 00:55:50,805
on ourselves and other people.

719
00:55:51,848 --> 00:55:53,349
They're for Him, too.

720
00:55:55,268 --> 00:55:57,062
Our purpose isn't

721
00:55:57,812 --> 00:56:01,524
just to make music that entertains people.

722
00:56:02,025 --> 00:56:04,402
Can't there be a deeper reason?

723
00:56:07,197 --> 00:56:10,867
When we were at our peak,

724
00:56:11,576 --> 00:56:13,953
we wasted our gifts on the wrong thing.

725
00:56:14,621 --> 00:56:16,623
We wasted them on personal goals.

726
00:56:17,665 --> 00:56:19,793
And being rockstars went to our heads.

727
00:56:23,088 --> 00:56:24,297
For a time,

728
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:28,885
we relied on ourselves so much
that we forgot about Him.

729
00:56:30,512 --> 00:56:32,764
Maybe that's how we lost the band.

730
00:56:32,847 --> 00:56:35,558
Because we didn't fulfill its purpose.

731
00:56:38,019 --> 00:56:40,021
Why do you think music exists?

732
00:56:40,522 --> 00:56:42,273
Why do you think we exist?

733
00:56:43,650 --> 00:56:45,693
Isn't this all for Him?

734
00:56:47,987 --> 00:56:49,948
So why don't we do everything…

735
00:56:50,031 --> 00:56:51,241
for Him?

736
00:56:54,035 --> 00:56:55,995
Make your life mean something.

737
00:56:56,955 --> 00:56:58,540
And use it wisely.

738
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:01,501
Use it wisely.

739
00:57:01,584 --> 00:57:02,544
Okay?

740
00:57:19,227 --> 00:57:21,729
Have you thought about Pao's question yet?

741
00:57:25,525 --> 00:57:26,568
What question?

742
00:57:28,027 --> 00:57:29,279
About music…

743
00:57:29,362 --> 00:57:31,781
And where it all comes from.

744
00:57:32,282 --> 00:57:33,950
And why we play.

745
00:57:39,247 --> 00:57:40,248
Have you?

746
00:57:40,748 --> 00:57:42,208
Did you find your answer?

747
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:45,253
Not yet.

748
00:57:46,838 --> 00:57:48,423
What about you? Do you have an answer?

749
00:57:57,348 --> 00:57:58,725
Do you remember this?

750
00:58:27,128 --> 00:58:30,757
<i>Used to like the sound of the rain</i>

751
00:58:30,840 --> 00:58:34,052
<i>And feel your arms around me</i>

752
00:58:35,094 --> 00:58:37,680
<i>Together we go insane</i>

753
00:58:37,764 --> 00:58:42,477
<i>But I wake up to where I should be</i>

754
00:58:42,560 --> 00:58:45,522
<i>I've longed for the wind</i>

755
00:58:45,605 --> 00:58:50,443
<i>They touch me through my feelings</i>

756
00:58:51,152 --> 00:58:54,781
<i>And you'll never know till they begin</i>

757
00:58:54,864 --> 00:58:59,911
<i>What you want is really what it means</i>

758
00:58:59,994 --> 00:59:03,039
Do you know why
we named the band "Sinagtala"?

759
00:59:03,831 --> 00:59:07,252
<i>Don't wanna be forever blue</i>

760
00:59:07,335 --> 00:59:10,838
<i>'Cause I deserve some love that's true</i>

761
00:59:10,922 --> 00:59:12,173
Don't you think it's weird?

762
00:59:12,257 --> 00:59:14,551
I never see the stars when we're together.

763
00:59:15,385 --> 00:59:17,679
Maybe that means we aren't meant to be.

764
00:59:19,305 --> 00:59:21,099
I don't think we need them, anyway.

765
00:59:22,850 --> 00:59:24,686
You're my star light.

766
00:59:25,186 --> 00:59:26,479
You're the brightest thing there is.

767
00:59:26,563 --> 00:59:31,276
<i>Cause I'm afraid, I'm afraid I'm afraid</i>

768
00:59:31,359 --> 00:59:34,153
<i>To be forever blue</i>

769
00:59:34,237 --> 00:59:38,241
<i>Gonna find some other guy for me</i>

770
00:59:38,324 --> 00:59:41,786
<i>This time it will be just like the wind</i>

771
00:59:41,869 --> 00:59:45,873
<i>Coming at the time it must be</i>

772
00:59:45,957 --> 00:59:49,377
<i>And blowing to where I should be</i>

773
00:59:49,460 --> 00:59:52,505
<i>I've longed for the wind</i>

774
00:59:52,589 --> 00:59:56,092
<i>They touch me through my feelings</i>

775
00:59:56,175 --> 00:59:59,762
<i>And you'll never know till they begin</i>

776
00:59:59,846 --> 01:00:06,436
<i>What you want is really what it means</i>

777
01:00:08,563 --> 01:00:12,066
<i>Don't wanna be forever blue</i>

778
01:00:12,150 --> 01:00:15,612
<i>'Cause I deserve some love that's true</i>

779
01:00:15,695 --> 01:00:19,157
<i>Finding it the hard way</i>

780
01:00:19,240 --> 01:00:23,661
<i>And wishing for it every day</i>

781
01:00:23,745 --> 01:00:30,209
<i>I guess I was wrong to want you, yeah</i>

782
01:00:30,710 --> 01:00:36,007
<i>'Cause I'm afraid, I'm afraid, I'm afraid</i>

783
01:00:36,090 --> 01:00:39,010
<i>To be forever blue</i>

784
01:00:39,093 --> 01:00:45,892
<i>Don't wanna be alone</i>
<i>I need someone to hold on to</i>

785
01:00:45,975 --> 01:00:50,647
<i>And share my dreams with a love, a love</i>

786
01:00:50,730 --> 01:00:55,693
<i>That's always true</i>

787
01:00:56,194 --> 01:00:59,656
<i>Don't wanna be forever blue</i>

788
01:00:59,739 --> 01:01:03,201
<i>'Cause I deserve some love that's true</i>

789
01:01:03,284 --> 01:01:06,788
<i>Finding it the hard way</i>

790
01:01:06,871 --> 01:01:11,334
<i>And wishing for it every day</i>

791
01:01:11,417 --> 01:01:17,590
<i>I guess I was wrong to want you, yeah</i>

792
01:01:18,341 --> 01:01:23,680
<i>'Cause I'm afraid, I'm afraid, I'm afraid</i>

793
01:01:23,763 --> 01:01:27,809
<i>To be forever</i>

794
01:01:27,892 --> 01:01:34,023
<i>Blue</i>

795
