1099
01:29:29,280 --> 01:29:30,656
Why, Dad?

1100
01:29:32,200 --> 01:29:33,785
Did anything even change?!

1101
01:29:35,745 --> 01:29:36,996
I'm still your son!

1102
01:29:37,080 --> 01:29:38,790
Your pride and joy!

1103
01:29:38,873 --> 01:29:42,293
Just because I came out
you don't love me anymore?!

1104
01:29:42,376 --> 01:29:43,836
Shut up!

1105
01:29:43,920 --> 01:29:45,338
Finish the game!

1106
01:29:45,421 --> 01:29:48,716
If you lose, you lose!

1107
01:30:18,913 --> 01:30:20,665
Do you think anything has changed?

1108
01:30:23,209 --> 01:30:26,462
You think I don't love you anymore
just because you're gay?

1109
01:30:30,633 --> 01:30:32,135
That's where you're wrong.

1110
01:30:58,452 --> 01:31:01,372
STAFF SUPPORT SERVICES

1111
01:31:10,673 --> 01:31:12,341
June, it's not looking good.

1112
01:31:23,186 --> 01:31:25,062
Hi, Mikey.

1113
01:31:26,105 --> 01:31:28,816
I'm your Tita June. Do you remember me?

1114
01:31:29,483 --> 01:31:33,237
Tita June, will you pray with me?

1115
01:31:37,283 --> 01:31:39,118
<i>While we prayed,</i>

1116
01:31:40,161 --> 01:31:42,330
<i>I asked Paola, too.</i>

1117
01:31:44,332 --> 01:31:45,499
I said to her…

1118
01:31:47,668 --> 01:31:48,920
"Pao…"

1119
01:31:49,420 --> 01:31:51,797
"If you're here, if you can hear us…"

1120
01:31:54,300 --> 01:31:56,135
"Take care of Reggie."

1121
01:31:59,263 --> 01:32:02,183
"You ask God for us. Tell him…"

1122
01:32:04,018 --> 01:32:07,104
"To forgive that stubborn fool."

1123
01:32:12,360 --> 01:32:14,737
"Because his daughter needs him."

1124
01:32:17,365 --> 01:32:19,784
At the hospital,

1125
01:32:24,789 --> 01:32:27,166
something happened that
I didn't tell the band about.

1126
01:32:32,255 --> 01:32:34,006
<i>I saw Paola.</i>

1127
01:32:39,220 --> 01:32:40,429
She had--

1128
01:32:42,890 --> 01:32:45,893
She had someone with her
but I couldn't see who it was.

1129
01:32:51,190 --> 01:32:52,566
But I knew somehow…

1130
01:32:54,527 --> 01:32:56,279
God was with her.

1131
01:33:02,618 --> 01:33:05,579
They asked me
what I wanted to do with my life.

1132
01:33:11,585 --> 01:33:13,421
I said…

1133
01:33:19,635 --> 01:33:22,013
That I wanted to spend it
with my daughter.

1134
01:33:24,307 --> 01:33:26,767
To be honest, I should be gone by now.

1135
01:33:28,978 --> 01:33:30,271
<i>I wanted to run away from everything.</i>

1136
01:33:30,354 --> 01:33:31,480
<i>The struggles…</i>

1137
01:33:31,564 --> 01:33:32,815
<i>The shame…</i>

1138
01:33:33,399 --> 01:33:34,942
The responsibility…

1139
01:33:35,860 --> 01:33:37,320
Life…

1140
01:33:42,074 --> 01:33:44,577
But I heard Paola's song again.

1141
01:33:48,748 --> 01:33:51,459
It was even trending online.

1142
01:33:53,252 --> 01:33:57,131
That's when I realized
that it wasn't just me.

1143
01:34:00,718 --> 01:34:02,261
"What is music for?"

1144
01:34:06,265 --> 01:34:08,517
What is music for?

1145
01:34:17,109 --> 01:34:20,321
Music exists
to remind us that we're not alone.

1146
01:34:22,448 --> 01:34:24,742
When I'm playing my guitar…

1147
01:34:28,537 --> 01:34:30,623
<i>there are no more questions.</i>

1148
01:34:32,666 --> 01:34:34,335
There's no judgement.

1149
01:34:40,174 --> 01:34:41,675
I am loved.

1150
01:34:44,637 --> 01:34:46,430
And through my music,

1151
01:34:48,391 --> 01:34:49,809
I love them back.

1152
01:34:54,271 --> 01:34:56,107
Where does music come from?

1153
01:34:58,484 --> 01:35:00,528
From a place of love.

1154
01:35:02,279 --> 01:35:04,323
Primo's bandmate said,

1155
01:35:04,407 --> 01:35:06,617
that he wouldn't jump off the cliff.

1156
01:35:07,118 --> 01:35:10,913
That he'd wait for the wind
to push him off.

1157
01:35:13,165 --> 01:35:15,251
<i>Then Paola asked us.</i>

1158
01:35:15,751 --> 01:35:16,836
<i>What--</i>

1159
01:35:17,670 --> 01:35:19,338
<i>What is music for?</i>

1160
01:35:19,839 --> 01:35:21,882
<i>Why do we play music?</i>

1161
01:35:24,510 --> 01:35:26,971
My answer, is Primo's answer.

1162
01:35:29,765 --> 01:35:33,686
Music is the wind that pushes back.

1163
01:35:37,606 --> 01:35:39,483
To save people from the cliff.

1164
01:35:42,361 --> 01:35:44,947
<i>I know that you may feel broken.</i>

1165
01:35:46,282 --> 01:35:48,909
<i>I was too when I found out I was sick.</i>

1166
01:35:50,661 --> 01:35:53,664
<i>But even feeling broken has a purpose.</i>

1167
01:35:54,165 --> 01:35:57,626
<i>That's how the Lord tells</i>
<i>you to take a time-out.</i>

1168
01:35:58,127 --> 01:36:00,546
<i>"Chill out and listen to me."</i>

1169
01:36:01,046 --> 01:36:03,591
<i>Because we all make mistakes.</i>

1170
01:36:03,674 --> 01:36:05,968
<i>We take a fall down the wrong path.</i>

1171
01:36:06,802 --> 01:36:11,515
<i>But the Lord cares enough</i>
<i>to guide us back to him.</i>

1172
01:36:12,183 --> 01:36:13,642
<i>To the right path.</i>

1173
01:36:15,269 --> 01:36:17,062
<i>Like I said,</i>

1174
01:36:17,146 --> 01:36:20,357
<i>"You cannot tell a seed</i>
<i>that it cannot become a tree."</i>

1175
01:36:21,400 --> 01:36:25,738
<i>"But a seed has to die,</i>
<i>in order to become that tree."</i>

1176
01:36:28,365 --> 01:36:32,870
<i>We have been broken</i>
<i>to fulfill our destiny.</i>

1177
01:36:35,998 --> 01:36:37,208
<i>Amazing, isn't it?</i>

1178
01:36:44,089 --> 01:36:46,509
Guys, we're about to start.

1179
01:36:46,592 --> 01:36:47,635
Let's pray?

1180
01:36:47,718 --> 01:36:48,552
- Yes?
- Yes.

1181
01:36:48,636 --> 01:36:49,762
Okay, let's pray.

1182
01:36:53,516 --> 01:36:55,017
Father in heaven…

1183
01:36:55,893 --> 01:36:57,311
guide our hands and our hearts

1184
01:36:57,394 --> 01:36:59,939
